+# Design
+
+## 对应需求
+
+FR-1 initial canonical transport; FR-2 strict free-helper reseal; FR-3 exact native dispatch and closed server receipt; FR-4 finite assertion/source correspondence; FR-5 fresh actual evidence.
+
+## 概述
+
+The actual constructor deliberately owns a copied canonical selection. Trusted test fixture metadata currently retains the pre-constructor object, while fixed metadata and ArtifactOwner paths require exact actual-client selection identity. Initial fixture adoption repairs that setup relation; it does not strengthen the data model or weaken any production check.
+
+## 技术方案
+
+IntegrationTLS uses one local adopt_selection helper. Before client entry it only replaces fixture Selection/Subject. After entry it requires an exact GitHub client, builds a fresh fixed fixture-token client, closes the old client, and adopts the new owned selection. seal and seal_final delegate to this helper. ArtifactAdmissionCases.fixture only assigns f.selection from its already constructed actual api.selection; f.api remains BudgetAPI data, and no native SessionOwner/ReadScope is synthesized.
+
+The POST method captures references to actual immutable snapshots only at the existing connection/sendall seam. It delegates the original successful send exactly once, records actual bytes privately, and asserts native snapshot/scope/client/credential/pending operation identities and consumed dispatch. It keeps the original post-header altered stream. Successful request headers are counted before and after the original terminal rerun rejection. Existing fixture exit performs its original joins; after exit, all server threads must actually be stopped, both original count assertions remain exact two, and original server rows are compared with actual private client writes. No new synchronization wait is introduced. Receipt output contains only allowlisted methods/roles, counts and successful proof booleans, never raw headers, body, tokens or credential hashes.
+
+This is the separately approved sixth method AST exception. It does not use the diagnostic last370B server row as identity or timing proof; that old row lacks target binding. The new assertions establish the complete target binding on fresh source. The original303 terminal outcome and305 effect-none hard rejection remain; original304/306 server count intentions are preserved after actual existing cleanup, with stronger zero-new-client-header proof surrounding the rerun.
+
+The two other once diagnostic methods were instrumented successful, not causal proof about the old full-run failures. Their old failures stay open. Extra readonly setter, foreign client, old two-argument authorizer and manual native activation methods are not included in this increment.
+
+## 文件结构
+Only this spec triplet and the four named test modules change. Production modules, existing source packets and all remote state remain frozen.
