+# Finite fixture canonical selection and POST receipt repair
+
+## 功能概述
+
+This is an isolated test fixture increment over exact fd3677436eb3811887befbd97d30fa54479200c6 (1871 tracked files), not F2 or release admission. The original whole300 has 215 named PASS and 85 non-PASS methods. Its failures and the later once-only diagnostic evidence stay unchanged. The diagnostic Archive and Source non-reproductions do not clear their original failures.
+
+## 需求列表
+
+## FR-1 — Initial actual-client canonical selection
+
+WHEN IntegrationTLS constructs its actual GitHub client, the trusted fixture SHALL adopt that same client's owned canonical Selection and Subject before metadata observation. WHEN ArtifactAdmissionCases.fixture constructs its existing third tuple actual client, it SHALL adopt its canonical Selection without replacing the client or treating f.api BudgetAPI data as a native credential, session or grant. Foreign clients SHALL remain foreign and selection value equality SHALL confer no transport identity.
+
+## FR-2 — Legal trusted fixture resealing
+
+WHEN an already entered IntegrationTLS helper reseals its synthetic selection, it SHALL construct a fresh actual GitHub client, retire the previous actual client and adopt the new client's canonical Selection and Subject. Before client entry it SHALL only update fixture data. It SHALL reject use with a model API, preserve production readonly fields, and add no fallback, manual scope, bearer grant or authorization. Only the existing seal/seal_final free helpers are migrated; extra method setter assumptions are separately recorded and are not silently rewritten.
+
+## FR-3 — Exact native POST dispatch receipts
+
+WHEN the separately approved OwnedRequestCases.test_post_dispatch_stream_drift_is_terminal_unknown_no_retry runs, it SHALL keep the original altered stream, real TLS, terminal uncertain_remote_effect and rerun hard rejection. Both successful POST headers SHALL equal the actual native immutable RequestSnapshot header and retain exact method/path, session/client/credential/op/scope identity, consumed scope and attempted operation. The rerun SHALL emit zero additional successful request headers. The original two server count-equals-two assertions SHALL be evaluated only after the existing fixture close and thread.join(3) lifecycle, without adding any wait or changing any deadline. Any live server thread SHALL fail the proof. Each original server method/path/header/body row SHALL equal the corresponding actual successful client writes in private fixture memory; header length alone SHALL supply no identity evidence.
+
+## FR-4 — Finite source and assertion correspondence
+
+The increment SHALL change no production source, request mutation classification, _safe, issuer, three hard rejects, snapshot suspension or PR98 cancellation boundary. It SHALL preserve all original test methods' AST except the explicit sixth POST method exception (the existing five exceptions remain separately recorded). It SHALL record the old303/305 outcome/rejection and old304/306 count intention correspondence without claiming the old server count passed. Existing budgets, old inputs, cleanup and no-retry assertions SHALL remain bounded and unweakened.
+
+## FR-5 — Fresh evidence and unresolved boundaries
+
+Before edits, exact same-source GitNexus upstream impacts SHALL be retained, including ArtifactAdmissionCases.fixture HIGH21 direct/1flow. Necessary tests SHALL use one new frozen source/runtime/runner/fixture and report every real failure/error, executed unique ID and cleanup result. No earlier 18/267/300/diagnostic component PASS SHALL be borrowed. Shared canonical setup corrections SHALL not by themselves approve additional method migration or classify all remaining failures as legacy. Final whole300 qualification requires a fresh complete run after necessary corrections; all unknown release prerequisites remain unknown.
+
+## 非功能需求
+
+No new wait, callback retry, budget extension, mutable grant or production change. Bounded proof output contains no raw request headers, body, tokens or credential hashes. Unknown remote body delivery is not inferred from successful client sendall or header append; any newly required complete-body comparison may fail and must be reported honestly.
+
+## 依赖关系
+
+AGENTS/probe4.0.1 and exact upstream impacts; actual GitHub canonical client constructor, original verified loopback HTTPSFixture, native held SessionOwner/ReadScope/OperationScope and registered ArtifactOwner. Earlier independent receipts are inputs for failure classification only, not new-source qualification.
