+# Design: native read scope and owned Stage composition
+
+## 对应需求
+FR-1 through FR-5 apply only to this detached F13cd draft. Unified patch b11462e8 and native patch08d16cb7 overlap only in executor/GitHub; their historical base bytes for those files are equal. The first union has29 changed paths and retains both fixed imports in the single adjacent-import conflict.
+
+## 概述
+Native GitHub owns canonical credential/Selection data and a held-loop ReadScope. Artifact-owned Stage uses its fixed StageAPI adapter. These are real distinct internal objects; checking only direct StageAPI identity or only the current session callback is incomplete composition.
+
+## 技术方案
+Keep the native readonly session API and canonical Selection, plus metadata-first artifact staging and the complete post-stage admission block. Use the fixed native read-control helper inside artifact controls for a client permanently owned by a native session, preserving the original callback and stronger later controls. It captures the actual current ReadScope internally and clamps the first/native/callee deadline for retained-byte work, not only HTTP requests. No callback or supplied scope can replace that controller. Standalone controls and the optional None callback retain their original bounded behavior. (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3)
+
+Native owner entry and later controls poll the actual ReadScope before any caller hook. Only the three effect-none control codes cancelled, timeout and adapter_error translate to the established ConsumerError vocabulary; invalid scope and unknown/confirmed wire effects retain their original failure. Stronger callbacks must return None. Standalone entry and control ordering remain unchanged. (FR-3)
+
+Native control capture passes the original owned/session end to the fixed read helper before applying an incoming deadline. After its actual scope check, the callback checks permanent owner controls, then validates the incoming deadline and callback with the original budget helper. Only after that successful capture is the incoming deadline merged with the original native end. Thus NaN, infinity, booleans and nonnumeric inputs cannot disappear through min, and an expired caller cannot outrun the first native cancellation check. Fixed normalized ConsumerError callback codes are relayed as local effect-none wire control codes so later enclosing budget polls preserve their original vocabulary rather than normalizing them twice. (FR-3)
+
+The shared consumer budget checker reads only an already-loaded ModuleType publication module from sys.modules. It preserves an exact actual WireFailure with the concrete unknown/confirmed effect and its original identity/release/asset; every subclass, duck-typed exception, missing module or attribute/registry failure keeps the old standalone normalization. There is no import edge from consumer I/O to publication, authorization grant or callback retry. This narrow shared helper change has a CRITICAL upstream impact and requires existing consumer budget, Stage and native regressions on the same new source. (FR-3, FR-5)
+
+The request snapshot must still require the exact StagedAssets, retained handle, zero offset, ordinal and fresh digest. For the fixed artifact-backed Stage only, validate the exact actual session._artifact_owner type, private registry identity, entered/open owner, same Stage, fixed StageAPI, same canonical client/Selection and owner._session is that exact native session. Direct client-backed native Stages retain their original path. No other adapter or external owner descriptor qualifies. Existing snapshot/operation checks and pre-dispatch authorizer remain. (FR-2, FR-4)
+
+Use actual native run_until_pause preparation with the verified ArtifactTLS fixture. A test observer may inspect an entered owner inside the original full-authentication call and then invoke that unchanged authentication;58 unknown rows still block and all local owners retire. A real first native deadline expires after the final metadata GET while reading the original retained provenance handle. The current session deadline and caller inputs may be longer, but that original issued deadline cannot renew. No ReadScope or mutation scope is manually minted. (FR-3, FR-5)
+
+Controlled local request-byte tests, where necessary, use the existing fixed verified-loopback authority context and actual native operation loop. The unchanged production authorizer is exercised as a denial at the target retained-upload boundary. These local fixtures establish request/stream ownership only, not a live GitHub grant or candidate eligibility. Coordinate source-specific fixture migration rather than adopting mutable credential/selection assignments. (FR-4, FR-5)
+
+## 文件结构与验证
+Add this spec trio, a dedicated native Stage composition test module and a bounded consumer/native caller-budget module. Necessary production changes are restricted to _ArtifactOwner._controls, its native entry ordering, _RequestSnapshot.__init__ and the approved exact-effect consumer budget bridge after fresh exact impact and failure-first evidence. The finite ExecutorCases.session loopback fixture explicitly refreshes the actual registered owner's native operation controls before returning its existing synthetic gates; it does not create any scope or live authority. Record the complete source/runtime vector and all historical failures outside the worktree; do not update original frozen packets or qualifying profiles. Preserve the native module's existing file-size observation rather than inventing an unreviewed split. (FR-1 through FR-5)
