+
+## 需求列表
+### FR-1 Immutable credential and selection owner (Must)
+WHEN a concrete GitHub client is constructed, it SHALL own validated immutable credential bytes and a deep validated frozen Selection. Supported token/selection assignments SHALL fail; neither caller dictionaries nor connector roles SHALL mint authority. Credential bytes and credential-derived hashes SHALL not enter repr, diagnostics, JSON or persistent receipts. Fixed trusted source and no concurrent same-UID writer assumptions remain explicit; Python private fields do not claim resistance to injected privileged reflection.
+### FR-2 Actual session operation scope (Must)
+WHEN a mutation is prepared, only the actual fixed PublisherSession with its held lock, exact native pending/inflight operation, owned client, cancellation state and finite native deadline SHALL issue a one-shot scope. External callback, data record, other client/session/operation, disposed session, paused deadline or stale scope SHALL not grant dispatch. At most one attempt SHALL consume a scope.
+### FR-3 Exact encoded request ownership (Must)
+WHEN building a mutation, the fixed serializer SHALL produce one internally issued snapshot binding the actual credential owner/client/session/scope, exact method/host/path/version/headers/body and selected subject/operation. Authentication and dispatch SHALL use that same immutable owner and original snapshot bytes. Foreign, edited, copied, replayed or imported snapshots SHALL fail before mutation bytes. No arbitrary Authorization/header/URL/body importer SHALL exist.
+### FR-4 Retained upload binding (Must)
+WHEN building an upload snapshot, the implementation SHALL bind the actual retained stage handle, ordinal, asset/release identity, initial offset, file identity/size and expected digest; verify owned handle and fresh bytes before attempting; and count/hash the original streamed bytes. A retained descriptor does not freeze underlying bytes; drift after possible dispatch SHALL remain terminal unknown. No mutable buffer snapshot SHALL claim OS immutability.
+### FR-5 Permanent native controls and failure semantics (Must)
+WHILE authentication, metadata, TLS and dispatch occur, original native session cancellation/deadline SHALL remain active; caller controls may strengthen but SHALL not replace them. Recheck immediately before the first possible mutation byte. Pre-dispatch denial has no effect; post-dispatch failure remains sticky unknown; confirmed cleanup failure preserves confirmed identities. No retry/delete/compensation/importer SHALL be added.
+### FR-6 Unavailable production authorization (Must)
+WHEN real publication is invoked, _authorize, _remote_constraint and _authenticated_latest_absence SHALL retain their hard rejections. The authorizer interface SHALL receive the exact owned request/scope in addition to operation/subject, without accepting a caller approval or fabricated scope witness. Fine-grained/App/OAuth/classic live grant and tag CAS SHALL remain UNKNOWN until genuine sources exist. All eligibility, policy, core, Issue86 and canceled PR98 boundaries SHALL stay unchanged.
+### FR-7 Ten negative test classes and controlled local mechanism (Must)
+Tests SHALL actually execute credential/API substitution, cross-owner binding, forged input/callback, request edit, stream drift, native cancel/expiry, replay/concurrency, pause/dispose/import, TLS/redirect/missing grant and unchanged remote hard-block cases. Controlled local request-byte positives SHALL use synthetic in-memory credentials and verified loopback TLS only, bind a genuine native session scope, and explicitly grant no GitHub authority. No sensitive credential SHALL be acquired, persisted or printed.
+### FR-8 Reviewable draft evidence (Must)
+The deliverable SHALL include exact source/runtime/fixture/patch scope, actual loaded/executed/named tests and honest failures, impact/detect_changes limitations and transplant requirements. No historical CI, count-only receipt, final F2 or publication PASS SHALL be claimed. No commit or push SHALL occur; integration onto the eventual real F2 requires independent review, finite source admission and fresh complete candidate CI.
